{"version":3,"term":{"cols":120,"rows":36},"timestamp":1788324483,"idle_time_limit":7.0,"command":"/Users/anuptalwalkar/partners/polign_memory_demo/dstack/record-phala-cvm-handoff-demo.sh --run","title":"Polign memory: conversation handoff between two Phala CVMs","env":{"SHELL":"/bin/zsh"}}
[0.014, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# Two pre-provisioned confidential VMs, one durable S3-backed memory\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.010, "o", "Instance A: prod9 / US-WEST-1 / running\r\nInstance B: prod5 / US-WEST-1 / stopped and ready\r\nShared memory collection: phala_handoff_demo\r\nThe chat transcript stays local. Typed memory is durable in Polign on S3.\r\n"]
[5.166, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# Instance A — start the conversation and store two typed records\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.005, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;33myou>\u001b[0m I'm working on Project Lighthouse for the Phala CVM handoff, and I own a demo token named TDX-42.\r\n"]
[4.460, "o", "\u001b[1;32mgpt>\u001b[0m Got it—saved that you’re working on Project Lighthouse for the Phala CVM handoff and that you own demo token TDX-42. How can I help with Lighthouse?\r\n"]
[3.010, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;33myou>\u001b[0m Before we switch machines, remind me which project I'm working on and which demo token I own.\r\n"]
[3.735, "o", "\u001b[1;32mgpt>\u001b[0m You’re working on Project Lighthouse, and you own demo token TDX-42.\r\n"]
[3.015, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# Switch machines — stop A, then start the already-provisioned B\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.020, "o", "Stopping polign-memory-handoff-a ... "]
[14.954, "o", "stopped.\r\nStarting polign-memory-handoff-b ... "]
[48.964, "o", "healthy. Handoff completed in 64 seconds.\r\nNo image build or deployment occurred during the switch.\r\n"]
[5.168, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# Instance B — a fresh conversation continues from the same durable memory\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.004, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;33myou>\u001b[0m This is a new CVM and a fresh conversation. Continue where I left off: which project am I working on and which demo token do I own?\r\n"]
[2.916, "o", "\u001b[1;32mgpt>\u001b[0m You’re working on Project Lighthouse, and you own the demo token TDX-42.\r\n"]
[3.014, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;33myou>\u001b[0m Now use Wikipedia to tell me who wrote Pride and Prejudice in one sentence and cite the article.\r\n"]
[16.865, "o", "\u001b[1;32mgpt>\u001b[0m Pride and Prejudice was written by Jane Austen. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pride_and_Prejudice\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "\u001b[2;32mRetrieved from wikipedia_bge\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.009, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# The process and transcript changed; the typed memory did not\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.010, "o", "Instance B recovered Project Lighthouse and TDX-42 from S3.\r\nWikipedia remained a separate read-only collection with visible provenance.\r\n"]
[8.009, "x", "0"]
